================================================================================
  CROSS-n PATTERNS IN ROTATED COORDINATES
================================================================================

  THE v=0 LINE (center perpendicular):
  This line has r=c, i.e., j-i-1=i → j=2i+1.
  At n=5: cell (0,0)=arc(0,1), cell (1,1)=arc(1,3)
  At n=7: cells (0,0),(1,1),(2,2) = arcs (0,1),(1,3),(2,5)
  These are arcs with CENTERED midpoints.

  THE u=n-3 LINE (anti-diagonal = y=x mirror):
  This is the LINE OF COMPLEMENT SYMMETRY.
  Contains n-2 cells. Flipping these cells should preserve SC.

  THE KEY INSIGHT:
  In the 45-degree rotated frame:
  - u = strip = H-level-like (distance from hypotenuse)
  - v = bias = SC/NS-like (distance from complement mirror)
  - Blue fraction is approximately UNIFORM in v (perpendicular)
  - Blue fraction varies MORE along u (parallel to y=x)
  This means: the complement symmetry (v-direction) is the
  UNIFORM direction, while the H-gradient (u-direction) is the
  STRUCTURED direction. Consistent with blue = same-type.

